  "task": {
    "objective": "Two teams carry their finite native packets to the opposing base. Deliveries reward both teammates and penalize the opposing team; tagging, sensing and covering can alter the race.",
    "natural_termination": "Both packets have been delivered; otherwise horizon 112 ends the contest. Either zero or one delivery at the horizon remains a valid outcome.",
    "interaction": "Packets can be picked up, handed off, dropped by simultaneous tags and recovered. Two sensing charges per actor fund warmup scanners or local decoy-jammer cover. Partner radio reports are sampled from the preceding state on even clocks, with explicit age; they do not grant current teammate visibility.",
    "observation_access": "Current entities are visible within Manhattan radius 2 or a same-team active scanner's radius 4. Enemy-team agents, packets and scanners inside their own decoy's radius 2 resist remote scanning but remain locally visible. Decoy transmitters remain detectable by remote scans. Same-team transmitters are team-known. Walls block motion, not radial sensing. Inactive objects are hidden. Reports are visible only to their recipient; only own charge is observed. Map, bases, delivery announcements and scores are public. Raw full state is privileged audit data, never a role-view HUD."
  },
